I really like the chasm idea, and particularly as a Dungeon
sub-branch. It would add a bit more 'geography' to the dungeon, which
is a bit 2-dimensional.

Rather than Lovecraft this instantly made me think of the Lord of the
Rings.

> Level 3: Ledges and rooms, presumably some unique challenge and reward.

I know LOTR is heavily used as source reference already, but I'd like
to see the Balrog restored to some of its literary menace. I've seen
lots of YAAPs with multiple Balrog kills and an "In your face Gandalf"
message. Given that when Balrogs usually appear in the game they are
just another tissue paper monster for high-level players, this is fair
enough, but trying to deal with one as an XL10-14ish character above
the castle wand? That would be a challenge: a bit like an early quest
nemesis, or the titan at Medusa's.

Maybe put the Balrog on a narrow bridge across the chasm. How do you
deal with it? Lots of choices: fight it, fly round (watch out for the
bullwhip), jump down (maybe he comes after you), get it off the bridge
somehow (scare it, confuse it, stagger it), make a hole in the bridge
(pickaxe, WoDigging, drum of earthquake) and make it fall in then
cross the hole by jumping... Hopefully enough variety and challenge to
make it an interesting add to the game?


btw, slightly off topic: why is jumping so restricted? Currently only
knights and boot-wearers can do it IIRC. YANI: If you get your carried
weight really low (i.e. you have to risk getting naked and throwing
your stuff across the gap first) couldn't all characters attempt a one
or two space jump? Perhaps have a variable success rate based on
strength and carried weight?

